# The repo's root .gitignore already covers dashboard/node_modules/, .next/, out/ and
# .env* (SPEC.md §2.4). This file covers only what is generated inside dashboard/ and was
# not foreseen there.

# TypeScript incremental build state
*.tsbuildinfo

# Vitest / coverage output
coverage/

# NOT ignored, deliberately: AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md.
#
# `next dev` writes them (node_modules/next/dist/server/lib/generate-agent-files.js) and
# re-adds them if deleted, so ignoring them means permanent untracked churn that no
# `git status` will ever surface. AGENTS.md is marker-delimited — Next manages only the
# text between BEGIN:nextjs-agent-rules and END:nextjs-agent-rules — so the file is stable
# and project-specific notes can be added outside the markers. It is also a real input to
# the remaining agent-run steps: it tells a fresh agent that this is Next 16, not the
# Next.js in its training data, and to read node_modules/next/dist/docs/ first.
#
# A blanket `CLAUDE.md` pattern here would additionally swallow a hand-written
# dashboard/CLAUDE.md if anyone ever adds one, on a project whose §2.4 talks about
# CLAUDE.md files. Ruled at step-1 reconciliation; see pipeline/steps/01-scaffold/.

# python bytecode from the regression harnesses — regenerated on every run
__pycache__/
*.pyc
